## Context
Output directories are an ad-hoc soup of file types: model replies
(`{slug}-run{N}.json`), extracted CSVs, `.record.json` eval records,
`_summary.json` files, `tavily_cache.json`, `self_consistency_summary.json`.
Every consumer re-invents its own filter:

- extract.py:362 — blacklists `.eval.json` (ticket 0043)
- self_consistency.py:144 — regex whitelist for `-runN.json` (already safe)
- analyze_multiturn_budget.py:25 — no filter at all (latent bug)
- Makefile:151 — `filter-out %.record.json` (yet another ad-hoc exclusion)

Ticket 0043 patched one suffix. The next derived file type (`.record.json`
already exists, `_summary.json` is coming from verify.py) will break another
consumer. Blacklisting suffixes is whack-a-mole. The harness already defines
the canonical output naming convention in `harness.output_filename`:
`{slug}-run{N}.json`. That is the whitelist.

The bug is latent today — no `.eval.json` files currently exist in output
directories. This is post-conference work (April 11 deadline), but the fix
is small and eliminates the entire class of file-confusion bugs.

## Actions
1. Add `iter_model_replies(dir: Path) -> Iterator[Path]` to `harness.py`.
   Implementation: `dir.glob("*.json")` filtered by
   `re.match(r"^.+-run\d+\.json$", f.name)`. This is the single source of
   truth for "what is a model reply file."
2. Replace `extract.py:362` glob+blacklist with `iter_model_replies()`.
   Delete the `.eval.json` special-case — whitelist subsumes it.
3. Replace `analyze_multiturn_budget.py:25` raw glob with
   `iter_model_replies()`. This closes the latent bug.
4. `self_consistency.py:144` already uses an equivalent regex — optionally
   refactor to use the shared function, or leave it (it is already safe).
5. Add a test: place `model-run1.json`, `model-run1.record.json`,
   `model-run1.eval.json`, `tavily_cache.json`, and `summary.json` in a
   temp dir. Assert `iter_model_replies()` returns only `model-run1.json`.

## Test
```python
def test_iter_model_replies_filters_derived_files(tmp_path):
    (tmp_path / "deepseek-v3.2-run1.json").write_text("{}")
    (tmp_path / "deepseek-v3.2-run1.record.json").write_text("{}")
    (tmp_path / "deepseek-v3.2-run1.eval.json").write_text("{}")
    (tmp_path / "tavily_cache.json").write_text("{}")
    (tmp_path / "self_consistency_summary.json").write_text("{}")
    result = list(iter_model_replies(tmp_path))
    assert [f.name for f in result] == ["deepseek-v3.2-run1.json"]
```

## Exit criteria
- Single `iter_model_replies()` function in harness.py
- extract.py and analyze_multiturn_budget.py use it (no ad-hoc globs)
- Test proves derived file types are excluded by default
- No module loads non-reply JSON by accident, now or when new derived
  file types are added in the future
